#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:4
msgid "3.x Changelog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:25
msgid ""
"Trio is no longer supported. ``set_trio_capacity_limiter`` and "
"``get_trio_capacity_limiter`` are removed from :mod:`litestar.concurrency`, "
"along with ``litestar.types.AnyIOBackend`` and the ``backend`` parameter "
"of :class:`~litestar.testing.TestClient` "
"and :func:`~litestar.testing.create_test_client`. :func:`~litestar.concurrency.sync_to_thread` "
"raises ``RuntimeError`` when called from trio. ``sniffio`` is no longer a "
"dependency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:168
msgid ""
"Every ``asgi`` handler, mounted or not, now receives a copy of the ASGI "
"``scope``, so the wrapped application can no longer add, replace or remove "
"top-level scope keys seen by the outer application. The default was "
"``None``, which passed the original scope through, warned at registration "
"and warned again when the wrapped application mutated the scope; both "
"warnings are gone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:174
msgid ""
"The copy is shallow, so nested values such as ``scope[\"state\"]`` are still "
"shared with the outer scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:177
msgid ""
"Set ``copy_scope=False`` where the wrapped application is meant to "
"communicate with the outer application through the scope, for example by "
"writing ``scope[\"user\"]`` for outer middleware to read, or by calling "
"``Request.set_session`` or ``Request.clear_session``. All of these now fail "
"silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:187
msgid ""
"Declaring a ``DTOField`` through Pydantic's ``Field.extra``, that is "
"``Field(**dto_field(\"read-only\"))``, is no longer supported. The mark was "
"already ignored in 2.x and only emitted a deprecation warning. Remove the "
"declaration and use ``Annotated[int, DTOField(mark=\"read-only\")]`` "
"instead; leaving it in place can make OpenAPI schema generation fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:216
msgid ""
"Declaring the \"reserved kwargs\" ``body``, ``cookies``, ``data``, "
"``headers``, ``query``, ``request``, ``scope`` and ``socket`` without the "
"type listed below, or with a different one, "
"raises :class:`~litestar.exceptions.ImproperlyConfiguredException` at "
"startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:221
msgid ""
"For this, add the "
"types :data:`~litestar.params.RawBody`, :data:`~litestar.params.QueryParams` "
"and :data:`~litestar.params.RequestCookies`, and the body "
"marker :data:`~litestar.params.RequestBody`, which declares a body of the "
"default media type, ``application/json``."
msgstr ""

