msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.attrs`` module. Code still using "
"imports from this module should switch to using ``litestar.plugins.attrs``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:893
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.jwt`` module. Code still using "
"imports from this module should switch to using ``litestar.security.jwt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:902
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.repository`` module. Code still "
"using imports from this module should switch to using "
"``litestar.repository``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:911
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.pydantic`` module. Code still using "
"imports from this module should switch to using "
"``litestar.plugins.pydantic``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:920
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated module ``litestar.contrib.minijnja``. This module was "
"created with a typo in its name (`minijnja` instead of `minijinja`). Instead "
"``litestar.contrib.minijinja`` should be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:928
msgid ""
"New ``round_trip: bool`` parameter to ``PydanticPlugin`` allows serializing "
"types like ``pydanctic.Json`` correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:938
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated ``litestar.contrib.minijinja.minijinja_from_state`` "
"function. Instead use a callable that receives the minijinja ``State`` "
"object as first argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:947
msgid ""
"Use ``litestar[piccolo]`` extra installation target and ``litestar_piccolo`` "
"plugin instead: https://github.com/litestar-org/litestar-piccolo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:957
msgid ""
"Move the OpenTelemetry integration from ``litestar.contrib.opentelemetry`` "
"to ``litestar.plugins.opentelemetry``. Code still using imports from the old "
"module should switch to the new path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:961
msgid ""
":class:`~litestar.plugins.opentelemetry.OpenTelemetryConfig` has been "
"brought in line with the upstream "
"``opentelemetry.instrumentation.asgi.OpenTelemetryMiddleware`` "
"configuration, adding ``client_request_hook_handler``, "
"``client_response_hook_handler``, ``tracer``, ``exclude``, "
"``exclude_opt_key``, ``exclude_urls_env_key``, ``exclude_spans``, "
"``http_capture_headers_server_request``, "
"``http_capture_headers_server_response``, and "
"``http_capture_headers_sanitize_fields``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:970
msgid ""
"Also fixes a ``KeyError: 'route_handler'`` raised on every request when "
"``exclude_opt_key`` was set, and corrects the ``OpenTelemetryHookHandler`` "
"signature to accept the span, ASGI scope, and ASGI message as documented by "
"upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:987
msgid ""
"Middlewares inheriting "
"from :class:`~litestar.middleware.base.ASGIMiddleware` will now have zero "
"runtime cost when they are excluded e.g. via the ``scope`` or "
"``exclude_opt_key`` options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:991
msgid ""
"Previously, the base middleware was always being invoked for every request, "
"evaluating the exclusion criteria, and then calling the user defined "
"middleware functions. If a middleware had defined ``scopes = "
"(ScopeType.HTTP,)``, it would still be called for *every* request, "
"regardless of the scope type. Only for requests with the type ``HTTP``, it "
"would then call the user's function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:998
msgid "This behaviour is still true for the legacy ``AbstractMiddleware``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1000
msgid ""
"With *zero cost exclusion*, the exclusion is being evaluated statically. At "
"app creation time, when route handlers are registered and their middleware "
"stacks are being built, a middleware that is to be excluded will simply not "
"be included in the stack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1006
msgid ""
"Even though this change is marked as breaking, no runtime behaviour "
"difference is expected. Some test cases may break though if they relied on "
"the fact that the middleware wrapper created by ``ASGIMiddleware`` was "
"always being called"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1016
msgid "Support unwrapping ``ReadOnly`` type in schemas like:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1018
msgid ""
"from typing import ReadOnly, TypedDict\n"
"\n"
"class User(TypedDict):\n"
"    id: ReadOnly[int]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1025
msgid ""
"``typing_extensions.ReadOnly`` should be used for python versions <3.13."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1032
msgid ""
"Add a new "
"attribute :attr:`~litestar.middleware.ASGIMiddleware.should_bypass_for_scope`; "
"A callable which takes in a :class:`~litestar.types.Scope` and returns a "
"boolean to indicate whether to bypass the middleware for the current request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:13
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that, on a route with middleware, an exception that no exception "
"handler creates a response for, ``after_exception`` hooks and "
"``pdb_on_exception`` would be called multiple times (once by the exception "
"handling layer of the middleware and once by the application's)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:18
msgid "They are called exactly once per exception instance now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:36
msgid ""
"Fix a bug, causing a Pydantic model used as a dependency to fail at startup "
"with ``Missing declaration for parameter`` for each of its fields without a "
"marker, since ``PydanticDIPlugin`` marked them as dependencies only in the "
"signature, not in the type hints used by the rest of the machinery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:45
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would implicitly give a field of an ``msgspec.Struct`` used "
"as a dependency a default of ``msgspec.NODEFAULT`` and mark it as optional. "
"Struct fields without a default are now correctly marked as required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:54
msgid ""
"Only the first ``cookie`` header was parsed "
"into :attr:`~litestar.connection.ASGIConnection.cookies`. Over HTTP/2 and "
"HTTP/3 the header may repeat, and browsers send one per cookie, so every "
"cookie but those in the first header went missing. All ``cookie`` headers "
"are now parsed, joined with the ``\"; \"`` delimiter :rfc:`9113` "
"and :rfc:`9114` prescribe."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:60
msgid ""
"A cookie name sent more than once now keeps its first value, where it kept "
"its last one before, following the :rfc:`6265` ordering that serialises the "
"cookie of the longer path first. Scope a cookie holding a session or a CSRF "
"token with the ``__Host-`` prefix so that a cookie of the same name, set "
"under a longer path, cannot take precedence over it. ``cookies`` "
"of :class:`~litestar.middleware.logging.LoggingMiddleware`'s response log "
"likewise holds the first of several ``set-cookie`` headers of one name, not "
"the last."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:72
msgid ""
"A session too large for one cookie is stored across several, named "
"``session-0``, ``session-1`` and so on. Over HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 only the "
"chunks carried by the first ``cookie`` header were read, "
"and :class:`~litestar.middleware.session.client_side.ClientSideSessionBackend` "
"yields an empty session when it cannot decode the value in full, so such a "
"session was silently dropped and the user logged out. Every chunk is now "
"read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:84
msgid ""
"The test client merged headers of the same name into one comma-joined "
"header, which is invalid for ``cookie``, and left a request carrying a "
"repeated header impossible to simulate. Repeated headers now reach the "
"application as they were given, on requests and "
"on :meth:`~litestar.testing.TestClient.websocket_connect`, which dropped all "
"but the last of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:90
msgid ""
"A test passing a header of the same name twice is affected: the application "
"now receives the two values it was given, rather than one comma-joined "
"value. Header values are also passed on as the bytes they were given in, "
"where they were decoded and re-encoded as UTF-8 before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:100
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would cause a request parameter typed ``Optional`` or "
"``Any``, *and* declared without a default *and* annotated as "
"``required=False`` to receive the ``Empty`` sentinel when that parameter was "
"missing from the request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:104
msgid ""
"A parameter annotated ``required=False`` that is consumed by any handler or "
"dependency, and does not have a default, now "
"raises :class:`~litestar.exceptions.ImproperlyConfiguredException` at "
"startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:108
msgid ""
"This includes a marker for a parameter also declared as a layer parameter "
"with ``required=False``. Layer parameters that are *not* consumed are not "
"affected by this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:116
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would raise :exc:`ModuleNotFoundError` when attrs or Pydantic "
"were not installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:124
msgid ""
"Fix a bug where ``ServerSideSessionBackend`` would store an empty session "
"under a new session ID and set a session cookie for every request, even when "
"that request did not have a session cookie attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:128
msgid ""
"The fixed backend will now only store a session if the client has a session "
"cookie set. Empty sessions for a request with a session cookie will now also "
"be deleted reliably."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:136
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that would resolve symlinks only for the directory path, not the "
"file path, when ``allow_symlinks_outside_directory=False``. The whole path "
"is now always resolved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:146
msgid ""
"A mount matched any path merely *starting with* its path string, so a mount "
"on ``/admin`` served ``/administrator``, handing the mounted app ``istrator/"
"`` as its path. A mount now matches only its own path and sub-paths of it, "
"``/admin`` and ``/admin/...``, and ``/`` still mounts everything that no "
"more specific mount claims."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:152
msgid ""
"Of several mounts matching a path, the longest one now receives the request, "
"so a mount nested under another, e.g. ``/admin/inner`` under ``/admin``, is "
"reachable. This also fixes mounts sharing a prefix shadowing one another, "
"and mount paths containing regex metacharacters, which raised ``500 - "
"Internal Server Error`` or failed application startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:158
msgid ""
"An application relying on a mount absorbing sibling paths that merely share "
"its prefix now receives ``404 - Not Found`` for them. Mount the application "
"one path segment higher, or declare the sibling path as a further path of "
"the mount, e.g. ``@asgi([\"/admin\", \"/administrator\"], is_mount=True)``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:197
msgid ""
"A ``websocket_stream`` handler whose function takes no ``socket`` parameter "
"adds one to its ``parsed_fn_signature``, but only to its ``parameters``, so "
"its ``original_signature`` lacked a parameter its ``parameters`` declared. "
"It now declares ``socket`` in both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:206
msgid ""
"A ``data`` parameter annotated with metadata, e.g. ``data: Annotated[int, "
"annotated_types.Gt(0)]``, was interpreted as a request body without a body "
"marker, which got around the check of ``data`` being missing a marker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:297
msgid ""
"A parameter whose name matched a path segment was read from the path even "
"when it was marked with ``FromQuery``, ``FromHeader``, ``FromCookie`` or the "
"corresponding ``Parameter`` kwarg, and was documented as a path parameter. "
"Such a parameter is now read from, and documented at, the location it is "
"marked with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:302
msgid ""
"A parameter named like a path segment that declares no location, the "
"deprecated inferred path parameter style, now raises "
"``ImproperlyConfiguredException`` when the application is created. Declare "
"it with ``FromPath``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:323
msgid ""
"Annotating a handler with a union whose members are all enums (e.g. ``Color "
"| Size``) crashed schema generation with ``TypeError: issubclass() arg 1 "
"must be a class``, as the union was dispatched to the enum schema handler. "
"Such unions are now documented as a ``oneOf`` with a component schema per "
"enum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:461
msgid ""
"``ResponseCacheMiddleware`` is applied per route, so a handler that never "
"set ``cache`` still had its responses written to the store when it shared a "
"path with a handler that did -- for example a ``POST`` handler on a path "
"whose ``GET`` handler sets ``cache=True``. Those entries were written on "
"every request, without an expiry, and were never read back, since responses "
"are only served from the cache for handlers that enable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:468
msgid "The middleware now passes such requests through untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:472
msgid ""
"Serialize subscription changes and consume notifications in a background "
"task so dynamic ``LISTEN`` and ``UNLISTEN`` operations no longer contend "
"with the listener. Psycopg 3.2.4 or newer is now required for development "
"and documentation builds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:634
msgid ""
"Fields typed as ``T | None`` (nullable) without a default value are now "
"correctly included in the OpenAPI schema's ``required`` array. Previously, "
"Litestar conflated nullability (the type can be ``None``) with optionality "
"(having a default value), causing the generated schema to diverge from the "
"OpenAPI 3.1.0 specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:639
msgid ""
"This affected all model types: dataclasses, msgspec Structs, attrs classes, "
"and Pydantic models. For example, a field ``name: int | None`` with no "
"default was previously excluded from ``required``; it is now correctly "
"included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:643
msgid ""
"Runtime request validation behavior is unchanged — nullable parameters "
"without defaults were already enforced as required at the validation layer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:719
msgid ""
"Fix the ``raise_server_exceptions``. This flag has been non-functional (i.e. "
"did not change the behaviour at all) since version 1. This is now fixed, and "
"unhandled exceptions will be re-raised by the test client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:727
msgid ""
"Fix a bug that could lead to unhandled exceptions raised within websocket "
"handlers, and not derived from :exc:`LitestarException` "
"or :exc:`HTTPException` to be silently swallowed. This would lead to a "
"closing of the WebSocket connection without any indication of an exception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:980
msgid ""
"Now, in the OpenAPI schema, ``pydantic`` fields with ``default_factory`` are "
"displayed as non-null and not required. Previously, this fields was nullable "
"and not required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release-notes/changelog.rst:1040
msgid ""
"Fix a bug in :class:`MsgspecDTO` where a KeyError was raised if "
"a :class:`msgspec.Struct` contained a :class:`~typing.ClassVar`. ClassVars "
"are now correctly skipped when generating field definitions."
msgstr ""
